      title: "IPC Church Website",
      video: "/assets/websites/ipc_website.mp4",
      description:
        "This website was developed for my church in India as a personal initiative while I was learning web development. The idea came from my desire to contribute something meaningful to the church using the skills I was developing. From planning the features to implementing them, this project reflects both my learning journey and my understanding of real user needs.\n\nThe home page features a hero section with a daily Bible verse that can be updated through the admin panel. The verse changes daily, allowing the site to stay fresh and relevant. I also implemented an image carousel to showcase highlights from each service, which can be updated regularly by the admin without redeploying the website.\n\nThe website clearly displays service timings, weekly schedules, and church location with Google Maps integration, making it easy for visitors to find information at a glance. A dedicated media page brings together live services and recorded messages, featuring YouTube video links and sermon content in an organized layout.\n\nThe core purpose of this website is the Songs Book feature. My church has around 1,000 songs used in worship, and I wanted to make them easily accessible in digital form. I built a searchable songbook where users can quickly find songs and view lyrics. The search supports Telugu and romanized text, is mobile-friendly, and includes voice search for faster access during services. Songs can be added, edited, deleted, and even imported in bulk through the admin interface.\n\nThe website also includes a Contact and Prayer Request page, allowing visitors to send messages or prayer requests directly to the church. Admins can configure the destination email and manage incoming requests easily.\n\nAn admin panel is integrated into the system, allowing authorized users to manage content such as verses, highlights, videos, songs, schedules, uploads, and site settings. This enables the church team to keep the website updated without any technical dependency.\n\nTech Stack\n\nFrontend\n\nReact 19 with Vite\n\nTailwind CSS\n\nReact Router\n\nAxios\n\nLucide Icons\n\nSonner (toast notifications)\n\nBackend\n\nFastAPI (Python)\n\nMongoDB with Motor (async driver)\n\nJWT-based authentication\n\nPasslib for secure password handling\n\nInfrastructure\n\nDocker for containerization\n\nNginx configuration for frontend delivery\n\nFastAPI handling file uploads\n\nEnvironment-based configuration for flexibility\n\nKey Use Cases\n\nPublish church updates, highlights, schedules, and featured content\n\nStream live services and organize media by category\n\nMaintain a centralized digital songbook with fast search and lyric display\n\nReceive and manage prayer requests and contact messages\n\nAllow admins to update content dynamically without redeployment\n\nWhy this project matters\n\nThis project represents my ability to identify real needs, design practical solutions, and implement a full-stack application from scratch. It also reflects how I learn by building, improving features over time, and adapting based on feedback and usage.",
      year: "",
